  "question": {
    "text": "Let the points on the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;be equidistant from the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Then the acute angle between the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "tZKKO",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>",
